# doorway/doorway-app — operator dashboard

What belongs here: dashboard views, the services that call the doorway's `/admin/*` and
`/auth/*` routes, and their TypeScript models. A new admin endpoint is added in three places
together (`CLAUDE.md`, "Adding Admin Endpoints"): the handler in
`doorway-service/src/routes/admin.rs`, the method in `services/doorway-admin.service.ts`, and
the types in `models/doorway.model.ts`. Admin routes are explicit handlers, never entries in the
dynamic route registry.

`covers: subtree` is a considered ownership claim with no edit-time rule. The app's gates are
its lint, format and test scripts, and the doorway service's own manifest governs the routes
this app calls.
